WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
A dry bean from the kitchen jar looks like a little pebble.

2
00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:05.960
It doesn't grow or move.

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:12.760
So is it alive? Two bags and a damp paper towel let your child find out.

4
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:20.513
Setup takes about twenty minutes, then two or three minutes a day for one to two

5
00:00:20.513 --> 00:00:26.353
weeks. Your child practices making a guess, waiting for a slow change, and checking

6
00:00:26.353 --> 00:00:30.773
it. And they find out that a dry seed is resting, not dead.

7
00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:37.317
You need twelve to twenty large dry beans from the grocery store, like lima, pinto,

8
00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:41.197
or black beans. Skip red kidney beans.

9
00:00:42.457 --> 00:00:47.657
Add two clear zip-top bags, two paper towels, a cup of water, a spoon, tape, and a

10
00:00:47.657 --> 00:00:48.657
marker.

11
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:53.230
Check for bean, pea, peanut, or soy allergies before you start.

12
00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:57.130
Keep beans and bags away from children under four.

13
00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.610
Stay with your child and count the beans out.

14
00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:04.010
If a child is choking, call nine one one.

15
00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.507
Raw beans contain natural toxins.

16
00:01:08.887 --> 00:01:10.567
Never taste a bean or sprout.

17
00:01:11.727 --> 00:01:15.187
If a child chews or swallows beans, call Poison Control.

18
00:01:16.547 --> 00:01:17.567
Look through the plastic.

19
00:01:18.807 --> 00:01:21.387
If you see fuzz, follow the guide's mold rule.

20
00:01:22.687 --> 00:01:26.607
Have an adult who can safely handle the bag seal it and throw it away.

21
00:01:27.867 --> 00:01:29.427
Never open or sniff it.

22
00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:32.873
Start by handing your child two dry beans.

23
00:01:34.273 --> 00:01:35.333
Ask, 'Is this alive?

24
00:01:36.613 --> 00:01:37.713
How could we find out?'

25
00:01:38.193 --> 00:01:39.893
Write down the answer in their own words.

26
00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.907
Fold a towel into each bag.

27
00:01:43.987 --> 00:01:46.947
Wet one with a spoon until it's damp but not dripping.

28
00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:49.667
Leave the other towel dry.

29
00:01:50.967 --> 00:01:53.787
Lay four to six beans a little apart in each bag.

30
00:01:54.807 --> 00:01:56.707
Label the bags water and no water.

31
00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:02.230
Before you set the bags aside, ask, 'What do you think will happen in each bag?'

32
00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:05.290
Have your child draw their guess and save it for later.

33
00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:09.587
Leave each bag open about a finger's width for air.

34
00:02:10.847 --> 00:02:15.487
Tape both to a bright window away from hot afternoon sun, or lay them on a counter.

35
00:02:16.807 --> 00:02:18.127
Check both bags daily.

36
00:02:19.447 --> 00:02:21.987
Add a few drops if the damp towel starts to dry.

37
00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.010
Here is a question for you.

38
00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:29.790
When the damp bean wakes, what do you think comes out first, the root or the shoot?

39
00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.250
And which way will it grow?

40
00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:40.643
In a warm room, most beans swell within a day.

41
00:02:41.863 --> 00:02:46.043
A white root usually appears in three to seven days and grows down.

42
00:02:47.243 --> 00:02:50.283
The curved shoot follows a few days later and turns up.

43
00:02:51.483 --> 00:02:52.903
The dry beans stay the same.

44
00:02:53.917 --> 00:02:58.597
After about a week, have your child predict what water will do to the dry beans.

45
00:02:59.997 --> 00:03:01.577
Dampen that towel and keep checking.

46
00:03:02.917 --> 00:03:06.737
Most of those beans will start growing, showing they were alive all along.

47
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.590
Compare the first drawing with the beans that sprouted.

48
00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.910
Have your child point to what matched their guess.

49
00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:17.370
At the end, count the beans back in.

50
00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:22.150
Throw the beans and towels away, then wash hands with soap and water.

51
00:03:23.217 --> 00:03:25.917
That pebble-like bean was never just a stone.

52
00:03:27.057 --> 00:03:29.377
It was alive and resting the whole time.

53
00:03:30.737 --> 00:03:32.017
Water is what woke it up.
